    <string name="region_info_title">Region Codes Explained</string>
    <string name="ps5_desc">• PPSA: Title ID used for Western releases and digital content\n• ELJM: Japan physical retail\n• ECAS / ELAS: Asia physical retail\nThe full code matters more than just the prefix because one PPSA family can still map to different regional builds.\n\nPPSA is broader than a simple single-region label. PPSA is the common PS5 title family for North/South American or European disc games and digital media, while Japanese physical games use ELJM and Asian physical games use ECAS or ELAS.\n\nA good example is the PS5 region guide for Cyberpunk 2077: it shows multiple different regional box codes all still beginning with PPSA, such as PPSA-03974 for the Americas, PPSA-04027 for Europe/Africa/Middle East, PPSA-04028 for Asia, PPSA-04029 for Europe/Oceania and Korea, and PPSA-04026 for Japan.</string>
    <string name="ps4_desc">A: Avatar | T: Theme | S: Social</string>
    <string name="ps3_desc">• B: Physical Blu-ray (C: Sony, L: Licensed)\n• N: Digital download from PSN\n• P: Vita Physical | U: PSP Physical\n• MRTC: Internal ID (Capcom/Asian) \n• NPIA: Internal ID (PlayStation Home)</string>
    <string name="ps2_desc" tools:ignore="Typos">PS2 keeps the same serial-style family as PS1\n• S: Sony\n• C: Sony / first-party | L: Licensed / third-party\n• P: Japan | U: America | E: Europe | K: Korea\n• Most retail PS2 games follow the same SCxx / SLxx pattern</string>
    <string name="ps1_desc">• S: Sony\n• C: Sony / first-party | L: Licensed / third-party\n• P: Japan | U: America | E: Europe | K: Korea\n• SCxx: first-party, SLxx: third-party</string>
    <string name="ps_mapping_footer">The PS1/PS2 mapping above follows Sony’s long–running product–code pattern.\nHardware region codes are recognized by the last digit of the PlayStation model number:\n0: Japan (Japanese boot ROM, NTSC:J region, NTSC Video, 100 V PSU).\n1: USA/Canada (English boot ROM, NTSC:U/C region, NTSC Video, 120 V PSU).\n2: Europe/Australia/PAL region (English boot ROM, PAL region, PAL Video, 220-240 V PSU).\n2A: Australia (bundled specifically with an Australian mains cord and composite RCA cable).\n2B: United Kingdom and Ireland (bundled with a BS 1363 mains cord and RF modulator hook-ups).\n2C: All other standard PAL European nations.\n3: Asia (English boot ROM, NTSC:J region, NTSC video, Wide range 110-240 V PSU).</string>
